8. MINOR NOTES
--------------
  - `clear log buffered` is accepted at exec and is what makes each leg's log readable in
    isolation.  Without it `show log` carries the whole day.
  - An "arp" grep over `show log` matches the IMISH command-audit echo of the tester's own
    `clear arp-cache`.  Match `ARP_LOG` instead.  A case that counted "arp" lines would have
    read a non-zero baseline and called the feature already on.
  - `terminal monitor` was never used.  It is exec-only and does not toggle (memory
    `terminal-monitor-exec-only`); the log was read with `show log` instead, which needs none of
    that and cannot leave a console streaming.


